  *   default (non-HS400) select, DLL held in reset, bus power with the msm
  *   BUS_ON power-IRQ handshake, CMD0/1/2/3/7 at <= 400 kHz, then 1-bit
  *   legacy speed (<= 26 MHz).
+ * Then (boot-arg sdhcspeed=, default 2) CMD6 to an 8-bit bus (1) and High
+ * Speed SDR at 52 MHz (2). CMD6 only sets volatile EXT_CSD mode bytes; each
+ * step is verified by re-reading EXT_CSD and comparing its read-only
+ * properties with the 1-bit copy, and undone (card and host) on any error,
+ * so a failed step leaves the previous, working mode.
  * Data moves by ADMA2 only: on this wrapper PIO reads of the buffer port
  * return the first word forever. All xnu RAM on sargo is above 4 GiB, so
  * the 64-bit ADMA2 format is used (SDHCI 3.0: DMA select 11b, 96-bit
@@ -114,6 +119,19 @@
 #define R2                      (RSP_136 | CMD_CRC)
 #define R3                      RSP_48
 
+#define HCTL_HISPD              (1u << 2)
+#define HCTL_8BIT               (1u << 5)
+
+/* EXT_CSD */
+#define EXT_CSD_BUS_WIDTH       183
+#define EXT_CSD_HS_TIMING       185
+#define EXT_CSD_DEVICE_TYPE     196
+#define EXT_CSD_PROPS           192     /* bytes 192..511: read-only properties */
+#define DEVICE_TYPE_HS52        (1u << 1)
+#define R1_SWITCH_ERROR         (1u << 7)
+#define R1_STATE(r)             (((r) >> 9) & 0xf)
+#define R1_STATE_TRAN           4
+
 #define XFER_DMA                (1u << 0)
 #define XFER_BCE                (1u << 1)
 #define XFER_ACMD12             (1u << 2)
